 r←Test_Server_416(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;uri;blocked;served;downloads;target;request;res;codes
⍝ Ask for files the server must not hand out: whatever the server itself runs on
⍝ ("Assets/Runtime/": Plodder, Rumba, certificates and their private keys), anything outside
⍝ the served folders, reached with ".." or one of its Windows variants, and anything in the log
⍝ folder that is not a usage data file, like the application log.
⍝ Files that are meant to be served must still be.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 uri←TC.ReplaceRegistryAlias'[localhost]'
 blocked←'/Assets/Runtime/Rumba/LICENSE' '/v1/Assets/Runtime/Rumba/LICENSE' '/Assets/runtime/Rumba/LICENSE' '/Assets/Runtime./Rumba/LICENSE'
 blocked,←'/Assets/../server.ini' '/Assets/CSS/../../server.ini' '/v1/Assets/../server.ini' '/Assets/..\server.ini'
 blocked,←'/usage-data/app-log.txt' '/usage-data/../Logs/app-log.txt'
 served←'/Assets/img/tatin.png' '/v1/Assets/img/tatin.png'
⍝ The JSON download of usage data files, which is what the client uses
 downloads←'app-log.txt' '../Logs/app-log.txt'

 codes←⍬
 :For target :In blocked,served
     request←R.NewRequest 0
     request.RequestTarget←target
     res←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
     codes,←res.StatusCode
 :EndFor
 :For target :In downloads
     request←R.NewRequest 0
     request.RequestTarget←Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/usage-data?download=',target
     request.Headers,←⊂'Accept' 'application/json'
     res←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
     codes,←res.StatusCode
 :EndFor
 →T.PassesIf∧/404=(≢blocked)↑codes
 →T.PassesIf∧/200=(≢served)↑(≢blocked)↓codes
 →T.PassesIf∧/404=(≢downloads)↑(≢blocked,served)↓codes

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
⍝Done
